.TH TENSOR_GPU_EMBEDDING 1 "November 2026" "Tensor GPU embedding handoff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensor_gpu_embedding.py \- stage protected embedding batches in the existing Tensor GPU queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ~/ops/shared/scripts/tensor_gpu_embedding.py
.RI [ --db " FILE" ] " submit | result | worker"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The submit command accepts JSON containing model and up to three inputs on
standard input. It stores private input bytes beside the existing queue and
returns an opaque job ID. The result command accepts a job ID on standard
input; it returns a completed, validated vector batch or a pending status.
Submit starts a transient Tensor systemd user worker when the job needs work.
The worker executes only embedding batches via local Ollama after the existing
GPU owner/idle veto and lease. A queued PDF ahead of an embedding waits for
the separate MinerU integration instead of being skipped.
No raw text or vectors are passed in command-line arguments or public Git.
.SH CLIENT MODE
Existing Nexus Qdrant writers and the Hermes knowledge-search MCP can opt
into the handoff by setting QDRANT_MEMORY_EMBED_COMMAND to a JSON argv array
for a pinned, noninteractive SSH invocation of this script. Without that
variable, their previous direct Ollama behavior is preserved. With it,
failures and the default 30-second bounded wait fail closed: no direct fallback,
Qdrant write, or writer checkpoint advancement is attempted. Configure every
writer and search consumer together only after a verified GPU-admitted worker
and protected transport are deployed.
Background writers may set TENSOR_GPU_EMBED_WAIT_SECONDS to an integer from 1
to 3600; the Nexus Qdrant unit uses 900 seconds so occupied-GPU jobs can wait
without losing their durable queue entry. Interactive calls retain the shorter
default unless explicitly changed.
Hermes `config set` may pass the same argv as a string prefixed with `json:`
to prevent its YAML parser from storing a list where MCP environment values
must be strings.
.SH PYTHON API
submit(db, inputs) deduplicates by operation/config revision and canonical
input SHA-256. run_admitted(db, claim, embed) requires a caller-supplied claim
and a separately verified GPU reservation; it is not an admission function.
The caller must keep the shared GPU reservation until the model is truly
released. result(db, job_id) checks the revision, digest, vector count and
4096 finite dimensions. The Nexus writers retain their own Qdrant exact-ID
readback and cursor rules; an embedding result alone never advances them.
.SH FILES
Private queue.sqlite3, payload-* and result-* files under the queue's
caller-owned mode-0700 directory. Never synchronize these files to public Git.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The Tensor worker and one local sample were deployed and verified on November
27. Nexus writer transport, real Qdrant upsert/readback, and MinerU dispatch
have not passed acceptance. Direct Ollama and MinerU clients still bypass this
queue. The worker does not force-stop a model possibly serving another client;
if it remains resident after the bounded poll, the lease is held for operator
recovery. Do not enable all Nexus clients before validating the SSH path.
